<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Technical appendices and supplementary material</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Implementation details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate SDN on top of GR00T N1.6 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> and Pi0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> policies for SimplerEnv, and GR00T N1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> for real-world experiments, without any additional training. For simulation, we use the official pretrained checkpoints provided by the original implementations. For real-world experiments, we fine-tune GR00T N1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>to adapt to our robotic platform. All SimplerEnv evaluations are conducted using a single environment instance. <span id="footnote1a" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            https://huggingface.co/nvidia/GR00T-N1.6-fractal</span></span></span><span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            https://huggingface.co/nvidia/GR00T-N1.6-bridge</span></span></span><span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
            https://github.com/allenzren/open-pi-zero</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In SDN, we sample <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=12</annotation></semantics></math> action chunk candidates from different Gaussian noise seeds. Each candidate is generated independently using the same conditional policy while varying only the initial diffusion noise. We then perform the Stage-1 grounding filter using kNN-based contrastive scoring with <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{6,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{6,10\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Based on the grounding scores, we retain the top-<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\{3,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\{3,5\}</annotation></semantics></math> candidates that are simultaneously closest to the grounded trajectory distribution and farthest from the perturbed trajectory distribution. For Stage-2 refinement, we evaluate the remaining <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> candidates using the kinematic smoothness metric JerkRMS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> over extended predicted action chunks. The extended chunk number is chosen to be greater than the executed action chunk in the environment, while remaining within the maximum prediction horizon supported by the base policy. For both SimplerEnv and real-world experiments, the extended chunk number is searched over <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{4,5,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{4,5,10\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Object Masking Strategy.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use Grounding-DINO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> to detect task-relevant objects and SAM2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> to track object regions across timesteps. We then construct perturbed observations using a simple masking strategy that overlays zero-valued bounding boxes over all task-relevant objects, effectively removing the target object information. <span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
                
                
                
              https://huggingface.co/IDEA-Research/grounding-dino-base</span></span></span><span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                
                
                
              https://huggingface.co/facebook/sam2-hiera-large-hf</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Selected Diffusion Noise (SDN) Inference</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
                
                
               Policy <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, observation <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, instruction <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
                
                
               Number of samples <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, filter size <math id="alg1.l0a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Initialize <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{i}^{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{i}^{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Generate <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{i}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{s},\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{i}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{s},\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Generate <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{A}}_{i}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{s}_{\text{neg}},\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{A}}_{i}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{s}_{\text{neg}},\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}\leftarrow\mathcal{G}\cup\{\mathbf{A}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}\leftarrow\mathcal{G}\cup\{\mathbf{A}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}\leftarrow\mathcal{B}\cup\{\tilde{\mathbf{A}}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}\leftarrow\mathcal{B}\cup\{\tilde{\mathbf{A}}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               Compute <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{ground}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mtext>ground</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{ground}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{i}\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{i}\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{M}\leftarrow\text{TopM}(\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>TopM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{M}\leftarrow\text{TopM}(\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{i}\in\mathcal{G}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{i}\in\mathcal{G}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
                Compute <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(\mathbf{A}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\mathbf{A}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}^{*}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{A}_{i}\in\mathcal{G}_{M}}S(\mathbf{A}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}^{*}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{A}_{i}\in\mathcal{G}_{M}}S(\mathbf{A}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                
                
               return <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Real-world experiements</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our method on two real-world robotic manipulation tasks using a single-arm mobile ALOHA robot. Each task is observed from both a <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">static camera view</span> and a <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">wrist-mounted camera</span>. Task definitions, initialization procedures, and dataset statistics are described below.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14084v1/images/realworld.jpg" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/150;" width="476" height="150" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>
<span id="A1.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Real-world tasks</span>
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14084v1/simulation_example.png" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/159;" width="476" height="159" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Simulation tasks in SIMPLER</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cube2Drawer.</span>
The robot first opens the top drawer, then picks up a red cube from the table, places it into the drawer, and finally closes the drawer. Each episode contains an average of 253 steps, and we collect a total of 150 episodes for this task.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Banana2Pot.</span>
The robot picks up a banana from the table, places it into a pot, then picks up the lid and closes the pot. Each episode contains an average of 280 steps, and we collect a total of 150 episodes for this task.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training and Evaluation.</span>
We fine-tune Gr00tN1.5 on the combined dataset for a total of 60k training steps with a batch size of 32 (approximately 20 epochs) and a chunk size of 50. Training takes approximately 7 hours on a single H100 GPU. During evaluation, we deploy the model on a RTX 4070 GPU and execute 10 actions per inference step. We evaluate 30 trials per task for each methods, with results summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 Real-world Experiments ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Self-Improving VLA Policies: Selected Diffusion Noise for Spurious-Robust Action Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Simulation Experiments</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our method on the SIMPLER benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>. For each method, we conduct 50 evaluation trials per task, and report the results in Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.2 Simulation Experiments ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Self-Improving VLA Policies: Selected Diffusion Noise for Spurious-Robust Action Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Simulation Experiments ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Self-Improving VLA Policies: Selected Diffusion Noise for Spurious-Robust Action Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Qualitative examples are shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ A.2 Real-world experiements ‣ Appendix A Technical appendices and supplementary material ‣ Self-Improving VLA Policies: Selected Diffusion Noise for Spurious-Robust Action Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. The evaluation consists of five tasks on the Google Robot platform and four tasks on the WidowX platform.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the Google Robot platform, we evaluate the following tasks:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Close/Open Drawer</span>: The robot interacts with a three-drawer cabinet. Given a language instruction, the robot must identify the target drawer and execute the corresponding opening or closing action.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Move Near</span>: Three objects are placed on a tabletop: a source object, a target object, and a distractor object. The robot is required to move the source object close to the target object.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pick Coke Can</span>: An empty Coke can is placed in varying poses on the table. The robot must grasp the can and lift it successfully.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Apple Drawer</span>: An apple is placed on top of a three-drawer cabinet. The robot must open the top drawer, grasp the apple, and place it inside the drawer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For the WidowX platform, we evaluate the following four tasks:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Carrot Plate</span>: A carrot and a plate are placed on a table. The robot must pick up the carrot and place it onto the plate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Eggplant Basket</span>: An eggplant and a basket are placed on a table. The robot is required to grasp the eggplant and place it into the basket.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spoon Towel</span>: A spoon and a towel are placed on a table. The robot must grasp the spoon and place it onto the towel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stack Cube</span>: Given two cubes, one yellow and one green, the robot must place the green cube on top of the yellow cube.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Compared to the baseline methods, SDN consistently improves upon the base model. We further provide a qualitative example in Figure <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ A.3 Simulation Experiments ‣ Appendix A Technical appendices and supplementary material ‣ Self-Improving VLA Policies: Selected Diffusion Noise for Spurious-Robust Action Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, where SDN enables successful task execution, whereas the base model without SDN fails early during the grasping stage and is unable to complete the task.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p">We further compare the effects of the grounding filter and kinematic stability refinement in SDN, as well as their sequential combination, with detailed results presented in Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.3 Simulation Experiments ‣ Appendix A Technical appendices and supplementary material ‣ Self-Improving VLA Policies: Selected Diffusion Noise for Spurious-Robust Action Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. The results validate the effectiveness of the proposed two-stage pipeline, which generally yields greater improvements than applying either stage independently. While the second stage primarily enhances kinematic stability, the first stage plays a crucial role in ensuring that robot actions remain faithful to task descriptions and in suppressing spurious action patterns. The sequential integration of both stages ultimately contributes to the strong overall performance of SDN.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14084v1/images/googlerobot_fail_success.png" id="A1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/173;" width="476" height="173" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>
Comparison of the base model and Base + SDN (training-free guidance) on SimplerEnv Google Robot
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14084v1/sim_ablation_two_stage.png" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/180;" width="476" height="180" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Performance comparison at different stages on simulation evaluation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Efficiency comparison between SDN and other methods.</h3>

<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14084v1/inference_plot.png" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/172;" width="286" height="172" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Comparison of per-step inference speed and task success rate across different methods.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ A.4 Efficiency comparison between SDN and other methods. ‣ Appendix A Technical appendices and supplementary material ‣ Self-Improving VLA Policies: Selected Diffusion Noise for Spurious-Robust Action Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> shows the per-step inference latency and task success rate across different methods. While baselines and CFG achieve faster inference speeds, they exhibit noticeably lower task performance. In contrast, SDN (Ours) attains the highest success rate of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48.33\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>48.33</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48.33\%</annotation></semantics></math> with a moderate inference cost of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="245.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>245.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">245.05</annotation></semantics></math> ms per step.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Theoretical Analysis of SDN</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide some theoretical insights into our framework under the behaviors of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="298.15" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 298.15" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,298.15) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 292.25 C 0 295.51 2.64 298.15 5.91 298.15 L 471.47 298.15 C 474.73 298.15 477.38 295.51 477.38 292.25 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 274.04 L 475.41 274.04 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 282.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Asymptotic Consistency of SDN Contrastive Grounding Score</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 252.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:17.26em;font-size:10pt;" height="248.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> be absolutely continuous densities on a compact support <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊂</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, bounded away from zero and infinity.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}=\{\mathbf{A}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\sim p_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}=\{\mathbf{A}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\sim p_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{N}=\{\mathbf{A}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N}\sim p_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{N}=\{\mathbf{A}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N}\sim p_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. samples.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For any query <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-nearest neighbor distances:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathcal{G}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}):=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j\in\Omega_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})}\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{A}_{j}\|_{2},\quad d_{\mathcal{B}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}):=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j\in\Omega_{k}^{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})}\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{A}_{j}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathcal{G}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}):=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j\in\Omega_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})}\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{A}_{j}\|_{2},\quad d_{\mathcal{B}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}):=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j\in\Omega_{k}^{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})}\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{A}_{j}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Define the SDN grounding score:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}):=d_{\mathcal{B}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})-d_{\mathcal{G}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ground</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}):=d_{\mathcal{B}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})-d_{\mathcal{G}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assume <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k/N\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k/N\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any fixed <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></span>
<span id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})=C_{D}\left(\frac{k}{N}\right)^{1/D}\left(p_{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}-p_{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}\right)(1+o_{P}(1))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ground</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})=C_{D}\left(\frac{k}{N}\right)^{1/D}\left(p_{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}-p_{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}\right)(1+o_{P}(1)),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{D}=V_{D}^{-1/D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{D}=V_{D}^{-1/D}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on dimension.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In particular, the ranking induced by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ground</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> is asymptotically consistent with the population score</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(\mathbf{A}):=p_{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}-p_{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathbf{A}):=p_{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}-p_{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">From classical <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN density estimation,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\mathcal{S}_{N}}(\mathbf{A})=\frac{k}{NV_{D}\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})^{D}}\xrightarrow{P}p_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbf{A})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑃</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\mathcal{S}_{N}}(\mathbf{A})=\frac{k}{NV_{D}\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})^{D}}\xrightarrow{P}p_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbf{A}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN radius.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})=\left(\frac{k}{NV_{D}p_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbf{A})}\right)^{1/D}(1+o_{P}(1))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})=\left(\frac{k}{NV_{D}p_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbf{A})}\right)^{1/D}(1+o_{P}(1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the average <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN distance is asymptotically equivalent to the radius,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathcal{S}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})=\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})(1+o_{P}(1))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathcal{S}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})=\rho_{k}(\mathbf{A})(1+o_{P}(1)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\mathcal{S}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})=C_{D}\left(\frac{k}{N}\right)^{1/D}p_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}(1+o_{P}(1))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathcal{S}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})=C_{D}\left(\frac{k}{N}\right)^{1/D}p_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}(1+o_{P}(1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting the expressions for <math id="A1.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS5.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="298.86" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 298.86" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,298.86) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 292.96 C 0 296.22 2.64 298.86 5.91 298.86 L 471.47 298.86 C 474.73 298.86 477.38 296.22 477.38 292.96 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 274.75 L 475.41 274.75 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 283.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Hallucination Suppression via Best-of-<math id="A1.SS5.p7.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> SDN Selection</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 253.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:17.31em;font-size:10pt;" height="249.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A1.SS5.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let the policy be given by:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}=(1-\epsilon)p^{*}+\epsilon p_{\mathrm{fail}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fail</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}=(1-\epsilon)p^{*}+\epsilon p_{\mathrm{fail}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mathbf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathbf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the population grounding score:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(\mathbf{A})=p_{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}-p_{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathbf{A})=p_{\mathcal{B}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}-p_{\mathcal{G}}(\mathbf{A})^{-1/D}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assume:</span></span>
<span id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(Consistency) </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ground</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> converges in probability to </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mathbf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathbf{A})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(Stochastic dominance) For all </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{A}\sim p^{*}}(R(\mathbf{A})\geq t)\geq\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{A}\sim p_{\mathrm{fail}}}(R(\mathbf{A})\geq t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℙ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℙ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fail</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{A}\sim p^{*}}(R(\mathbf{A})\geq t)\geq\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{A}\sim p_{\mathrm{fail}}}(R(\mathbf{A})\geq t).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Draw <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{A}_{N}\overset{i.i.d.}{\sim}\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">d</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.700em">.</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{A}_{N}\overset{i.i.d.}{\sim}\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and select</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}^{*}=\arg\max_{1\leq i\leq N}R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ground</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}^{*}=\arg\max_{1\leq i\leq N}R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}(\mathbf{A}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Then,</span></span>
<span id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{A}^{*}\sim p_{\mathrm{fail}})\leq\exp(-cN)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fail</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{A}^{*}\sim p_{\mathrm{fail}})\leq\exp(-cN),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">for some constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{fail}}\sim\mathrm{Binomial}(N,\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Binomial</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{fail}}\sim\mathrm{Binomial}(N,\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{*}=N-N_{\mathrm{fail}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{*}=N-N_{\mathrm{fail}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{fail}}:=\max_{i\leq N_{\mathrm{fail}}}R(\mathbf{A}_{i}),\quad M_{*}:=\max_{j\leq N_{*}}R(\mathbf{A}_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{fail}}:=\max_{i\leq N_{\mathrm{fail}}}R(\mathbf{A}_{i}),\quad M_{*}:=\max_{j\leq N_{*}}R(\mathbf{A}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A1.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(M_{*}&lt;t)=\mathbb{P}_{p^{*}}(R(\mathbf{A})&lt;t)^{N_{*}},\quad\mathbb{P}(M_{\mathrm{fail}}\geq t)\leq 1-(1-\delta)^{N_{\mathrm{fail}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(M_{*}&lt;t)=\mathbb{P}_{p^{*}}(R(\mathbf{A})&lt;t)^{N_{*}},\quad\mathbb{P}(M_{\mathrm{fail}}\geq t)\leq 1-(1-\delta)^{N_{\mathrm{fail}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\mathbb{P}_{p_{\mathrm{fail}}}(R(\mathbf{A})\geq t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\mathbb{P}_{p_{\mathrm{fail}}}(R(\mathbf{A})\geq t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By stochastic dominance, there exists <math id="A1.SS5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{p^{*}}(R\geq t)&gt;\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{p^{*}}(R\geq t)&gt;\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(M_{\mathrm{fail}}\geq M_{*})\leq N_{\mathrm{fail}}\delta+(1-\delta)^{N_{*}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(M_{\mathrm{fail}}\geq M_{*})\leq N_{\mathrm{fail}}\delta+(1-\delta)^{N_{*}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation over <math id="A1.SS5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{fail}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{fail}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields exponential decay:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{A}^{*}\sim p_{\mathrm{fail}})\leq\exp(-cN)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>fail</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{A}^{*}\sim p_{\mathrm{fail}})\leq\exp(-cN).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, consistency of <math id="A1.SS5.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>ground</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{ground}}^{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math> implies the same result holds when using the empirical score.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
